Meaning-search request construction, batching, redaction, spend budgeting,
and the Jev client are adapted from zachlandes/herdr-find, commit 4736dd5
(Apache-2.0), originally developed in Dewey.
Modified for general line input, shared key handling, durable
spend reservations, result caching and independent CLI use.

Meaning-search questions derive from Needle by Shubham Saboo,
awesome-llm-apps (Apache-2.0), via Dewey and herdr-find.
The inherited 0.58 match threshold also comes from Needle.
https://github.com/Shubhamsaboo/awesome-llm-apps/tree/main/advanced_llm_apps/needle

